WEBVTT

00:00:05.650 --> 00:00:07.940
Please eat your fill,

00:00:09.270 --> 00:00:10.190
Mother.

00:00:12.490 --> 00:00:16.780
Let's have our breakfast, too, Hibiki.

00:00:17.320 --> 00:00:19.200
Okay, Dad.

00:00:27.250 --> 00:00:29.670
It's your first day at your new school.
Will you be okay?

00:00:30.040 --> 00:00:30.750
Yes.

00:00:31.340 --> 00:00:32.670
Do you have everything?

00:00:33.260 --> 00:00:36.050
If you have any sort of trouble...

00:00:36.050 --> 00:00:37.340
If I have any trouble,

00:00:37.340 --> 00:00:39.600
everyone will be there to help.

00:00:42.770 --> 00:00:45.180
Okay, then. Be careful.

00:00:47.520 --> 00:00:48.560
Off you go.

00:00:49.940 --> 00:00:51.070
See you later.

00:01:51.130 --> 00:01:53.290
<i>She looks like a princess or something.</i>

00:01:54.880 --> 00:01:58.340
<i>I wonder if I'd look like her if I let my hair down...</i>

00:01:59.680 --> 00:02:00.720
Oh, yeah...

00:02:12.770 --> 00:02:14.900
I'm sorry! I'm just, uh...

00:02:21.660 --> 00:02:24.080
What are you doing?! That's dangerous!

00:02:25.370 --> 00:02:27.750
C'mon, let's get going.

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:31.170
Okay.

00:02:38.510 --> 00:02:40.170
Seriously...

00:02:40.170 --> 00:02:42.590
Did you hurt your foot or something?

00:02:42.590 --> 00:02:46.760
What if something had happened to you
right there in the middle of the street?

00:02:49.020 --> 00:02:50.810
Thank you.

00:02:51.270 --> 00:02:54.730
He was just playing a little joke, though.

00:02:55.020 --> 00:02:56.860
He didn't mean any harm.

00:02:57.980 --> 00:02:58.570
Huh?

00:04:58.900 --> 00:05:00.650
Come here...

00:05:02.870 --> 00:05:05.450
Come here...

00:05:05.450 --> 00:05:09.650
S-Sorry, but I'm on my way to school.

00:05:10.790 --> 00:05:12.500
I know.

00:05:12.500 --> 00:05:17.130
But as a soul bound to the place of my death, this is what I do.

00:05:17.130 --> 00:05:22.080
U-Um... I'll stop by again on my way home.

00:05:22.080 --> 00:05:23.460
Do as you please.

00:05:24.140 --> 00:05:27.680
You know, it's been about
a week since I last saw you.

00:05:28.430 --> 00:05:30.810
Have you gotten used to your new school?

00:05:31.520 --> 00:05:32.690
Yes!

00:05:35.060 --> 00:05:37.020
Thank goodness I wasn't late!

00:05:37.480 --> 00:05:39.690
Morning, Amami!

00:05:42.360 --> 00:05:45.320
Good morning, Ogawa.

00:05:46.490 --> 00:05:47.910
You too, Uehara.

00:05:47.910 --> 00:05:48.580
Hey.

00:05:48.580 --> 00:05:49.870
And you, Esumi.

00:05:49.870 --> 00:05:51.080
'Sup.

00:05:53.120 --> 00:05:54.380
Really?

00:05:54.380 --> 00:05:55.290
Yeah!

00:05:57.800 --> 00:06:00.720
Looks like Amami's finally warmed up to this place.

00:06:01.220 --> 00:06:03.840
She had a lot of trouble at first.

00:06:04.510 --> 00:06:05.390
She'd randomly start talking to thin air,

00:06:05.390 --> 00:06:07.140
Good morning!

00:06:07.640 --> 00:06:08.810
and then she'd skirt around invisible obstacles.

00:06:08.810 --> 00:06:10.220
Excuse me!

00:06:10.220 --> 00:06:10.770
and then she'd skirt around invisible obstacles.

00:06:10.770 --> 00:06:14.730
Yeah. She has that thing that
lets you see spirits. A sixth sense.

00:06:15.230 --> 00:06:18.440
I was a little creeped out by her at first, but...

00:06:21.440 --> 00:06:24.070
Don't push me!

00:06:24.070 --> 00:06:25.110
I guess we've just gotten used to it.

00:06:25.110 --> 00:06:27.450
Amami!

00:06:30.700 --> 00:06:32.830
Amami, are you all right?

00:06:32.830 --> 00:06:35.620
Y-Yes, I'm fine.

00:06:38.170 --> 00:06:42.420
I-I appreciate the thought,
but I can open doors myself.

00:06:42.420 --> 00:06:44.130
Every door is automatic for her.

00:06:44.130 --> 00:06:46.510
The ghosts must really like her.

00:06:46.510 --> 00:06:48.390
Hey!

00:06:48.390 --> 00:06:50.430
Good morning, Ama—

00:06:55.190 --> 00:06:58.060
P-Please wake up, Yamada!

00:06:58.060 --> 00:06:59.610
Hey, new kid!

00:07:00.270 --> 00:07:01.610
Inoue!

00:07:02.690 --> 00:07:04.320
Good morning.

00:07:04.320 --> 00:07:06.200
Don't give me that "good morning" crap!

00:07:06.200 --> 00:07:09.240
Come on, at least say hello to her.

00:07:09.240 --> 00:07:10.620
Sh-Shut up.

00:07:11.080 --> 00:07:12.500
Oh, screw it!

00:07:13.120 --> 00:07:15.370
I'm gonna give it to you straight right now.

00:07:15.750 --> 00:07:20.130
This "sixth sense" or whatever you call it is ridiculous!

00:07:20.130 --> 00:07:23.050
Wow, she's not wasting any time this morning.

00:07:23.050 --> 00:07:25.930
Inoue hates paranormal stuff.

00:07:26.930 --> 00:07:30.260
That said, why aren't you three bothered by any of this?

00:07:30.550 --> 00:07:33.310
Well, it's not like we can see them.

00:07:33.310 --> 00:07:36.270
Amami's the only one they mess with.

00:07:36.270 --> 00:07:38.100
We're sort of used to it.

00:07:38.100 --> 00:07:39.270
Yeah.

00:07:39.610 --> 00:07:42.940
I swear, every last one of you is totally nuts!

00:07:42.940 --> 00:07:45.400
Well, <i>I</i> don't believe any of it!

00:07:45.950 --> 00:07:47.490
U-Um...

00:07:47.490 --> 00:07:51.370
You're free to regard me however you like, but...

00:07:52.120 --> 00:07:54.250
I hope you'll believe your grandma.

00:07:54.250 --> 00:07:57.290
She's right behind you.

00:07:57.580 --> 00:08:00.540
Nana, are you there?!

00:08:00.540 --> 00:08:03.300
Inoue's a grandma's girl?

00:08:04.670 --> 00:08:06.920
You can't fool me with your lies!

00:08:07.420 --> 00:08:09.300
B-But...

00:08:13.600 --> 00:08:17.100
Stop following empty space with your eyes!

00:08:17.100 --> 00:08:18.890
Settle down, Inoue.

00:08:19.270 --> 00:08:21.900
Don't bully your classmates, or else...

00:08:21.900 --> 00:08:22.650
Or else what?

00:08:23.230 --> 00:08:25.990
Or else your beloved grandma will hate you.

00:08:28.490 --> 00:08:29.780
Gotcha.

00:08:33.660 --> 00:08:37.410
Nana would never hate me!

00:08:38.250 --> 00:08:41.080
Does she believe in ghosts or not?

00:08:47.130 --> 00:08:49.920
Hey, look! There's a cat!

00:08:51.720 --> 00:08:53.850
Isn't it cute?

00:08:54.350 --> 00:08:59.140
Come to think of it, didn't you say
you could speak to cats, Amami?

00:08:59.140 --> 00:09:01.730
Yes, but only a little.

00:09:04.860 --> 00:09:07.360
Whoa, a whole gaggle of chicks in bloomers!

00:09:07.360 --> 00:09:10.030
Can't get enough of those plump thighs!

00:09:10.030 --> 00:09:11.030
C'mon, what's the problem?!

00:09:11.030 --> 00:09:13.660
Don't be a prude! Lemme see!

00:09:19.160 --> 00:09:22.460
Wow! You're very good at this.

00:09:22.830 --> 00:09:25.500
A friend taught me how to cut them this way.

00:09:25.500 --> 00:09:28.300
Oh, I didn't know we had such a prodigy here!

00:09:29.090 --> 00:09:31.220
Yes, right over here.

00:09:34.510 --> 00:09:35.010
Huh?

00:09:38.770 --> 00:09:41.800
So, what is the person who taught you like?

00:09:42.300 --> 00:09:43.850
Well...

00:09:44.430 --> 00:09:47.110
She has beautiful hands, with long fingers.

00:09:47.610 --> 00:09:49.650
Why her hands?

00:09:49.650 --> 00:09:51.530
Wouldn't most people describe the face?

00:09:52.150 --> 00:09:56.950
Well, actually, she hasn't found the rest of her body yet.

00:09:59.410 --> 00:10:03.670
But I'm sure that her face is very beautiful, too.

00:10:05.250 --> 00:10:08.380
I can't hear you!

00:10:12.970 --> 00:10:15.390
What are you doing, Amami?

00:10:15.390 --> 00:10:20.300
Oh, I promised a girl who lives near me that I'd give her a handkerchief.

00:10:20.710 --> 00:10:23.260
I'm embroidering her name on this one.

00:10:24.260 --> 00:10:25.220
Who is she?

00:10:26.350 --> 00:10:31.070
Hanako. She haunts the toilet at West Gate Park.

00:10:31.400 --> 00:10:35.450
She finally brings up a name I recognize, and yet I'm not happy. Why is that?

00:10:35.450 --> 00:10:37.450
It's best not to think about it.

00:10:37.450 --> 00:10:40.080
Hanako is a very common name, very common, very—

00:10:49.550 --> 00:10:50.840
What's wrong, Amami?

00:10:51.170 --> 00:10:53.050
C'mon, tell us what happened.

00:10:53.550 --> 00:10:57.180
Yesterday, Hanako,
the girl I gave the handkerchief to...

00:10:58.050 --> 00:10:59.850
She disappeared!

00:11:00.310 --> 00:11:04.440
Her last words were "thank you"...

00:11:07.100 --> 00:11:10.360
Hanako went to the other side!

00:11:10.360 --> 00:11:12.650
She crossed over!

00:11:19.030 --> 00:11:22.200
H-How long are you gonna cry in here?

00:11:23.660 --> 00:11:25.870
She disappeared, that's all.

00:11:25.870 --> 00:11:29.130
You'll run into her again sooner or later.

00:11:29.960 --> 00:11:31.300
Inoue...

00:11:32.380 --> 00:11:36.050
J-Just so you know,
I don't believe in ghosts, okay?

00:11:37.670 --> 00:11:38.290
Right.

00:11:39.040 --> 00:11:40.590
Thank you.

00:11:48.800 --> 00:11:50.810
I'm in here!

00:11:51.110 --> 00:11:54.650
She followed you to school!

00:11:55.140 --> 00:11:59.980
Forget it! I'll never accept you!

00:12:01.120 --> 00:12:05.340
<i>The school is so creepy in the evening.</i>

00:12:05.340 --> 00:12:09.050
<i>This is when you run into things
you really don't want to run into.</i>

00:12:13.820 --> 00:12:14.830
<i>Why...</i>

00:12:16.790 --> 00:12:18.630
I-Inoue?

00:12:18.630 --> 00:12:22.550
Why did it have to be the new kid?!

00:12:24.010 --> 00:12:27.560
Um, why are you here so late?

00:12:28.690 --> 00:12:31.480
I-I'm the class rep. I had work to do.

00:12:32.020 --> 00:12:36.820
You're not going to tell me you're
hanging out with a ghost, are you?

00:12:37.320 --> 00:12:39.450
How did you know?

00:12:39.450 --> 00:12:41.320
You're not even trying to spin it?!

00:12:42.320 --> 00:12:45.870
We were all playing hide and seek, actually,

00:12:45.870 --> 00:12:48.160
but I can't seem to find any of them.

00:12:49.830 --> 00:12:54.090
Who plays hide and seek with things that are invisible to begin with?!

00:12:55.800 --> 00:12:58.050
<i>That's what I want to say...</i>

00:12:58.670 --> 00:13:01.800
<i>But I'm afraid it'll come back around to me twofold!</i>

00:13:04.260 --> 00:13:05.930
U-Um...

00:13:05.930 --> 00:13:07.140
Inoue?

00:13:10.600 --> 00:13:11.520
What is it?

00:13:12.190 --> 00:13:16.570
We both walk the same way to the station, right?

00:13:17.440 --> 00:13:18.320
Yeah, so?

00:13:19.450 --> 00:13:22.570
We walk... the same way...

00:13:25.450 --> 00:13:28.330
W-Wait for me!

00:13:35.170 --> 00:13:38.010
Hey there, ladies. Let's see those panties—

00:13:43.430 --> 00:13:44.760
Kitty?

00:13:45.180 --> 00:13:46.760
Are you all right?

00:13:47.470 --> 00:13:50.810
I... I kinda liked that...

00:13:54.350 --> 00:13:56.770
U-Um... Inoue!

00:13:57.690 --> 00:13:59.990
I'd really like to walk with you.

00:14:01.110 --> 00:14:04.660
Why? You'll be fine by yourself—

00:14:06.030 --> 00:14:09.040
She's not fine at all!

00:14:12.620 --> 00:14:17.540
Lately, the kids around here call for me a lot.

00:14:18.800 --> 00:14:21.720
Kids? What kids?

00:14:29.600 --> 00:14:33.310
What do you want to play today?

00:14:33.310 --> 00:14:36.360
<i>I knew it, and yet I still asked.</i>

00:14:36.360 --> 00:14:39.530
Inoue, would you like to play, too?

00:14:39.530 --> 00:14:40.650
No way!

00:14:41.780 --> 00:14:46.070
I-It's okay. Don't cry, kids.

00:14:46.070 --> 00:14:46.660
<i>I-I made them cry? I didn't mean to...</i>

00:14:46.660 --> 00:14:51.700
You don't have to be scared. It's okay...

00:14:52.450 --> 00:14:53.580
I'm sorry!

00:14:54.250 --> 00:14:56.540
I just remembered I have somewhere to go.

00:14:56.540 --> 00:14:57.040
Huh?

00:14:57.830 --> 00:15:01.420
I'll be right back. Please just wait here.

00:15:01.800 --> 00:15:04.170
Wait... At a time like this?!

00:15:09.850 --> 00:15:11.930
Wh-What are you so scared of?

00:15:11.930 --> 00:15:15.020
I'm a lot more scared than you are!

00:15:20.270 --> 00:15:24.490
What the heck am I doing,
out here with no one around?

00:15:25.700 --> 00:15:26.910
I'm leavi—

00:15:33.910 --> 00:15:37.080
Seriously, what's the deal with that new kid?

00:15:37.080 --> 00:15:39.630
Manipulating me like that...

00:15:43.840 --> 00:15:45.970
Will you play with us?

00:15:47.180 --> 00:15:48.470
Why should I...

00:15:49.010 --> 00:15:52.560
C'mon, it's past sundown already.

00:15:52.560 --> 00:15:56.060
It's dangerous for kids to be out,
so go home before it gets dark...

00:15:59.770 --> 00:16:01.820
O-Oh, fine.

00:16:02.230 --> 00:16:04.360
I'll play with you for a little while.

00:16:04.940 --> 00:16:06.190
Really?

00:16:06.190 --> 00:16:08.820
J-Just for a little while!

00:16:08.820 --> 00:16:12.030
We'll play for a bit, and then you're going straight home.

00:16:12.740 --> 00:16:15.330
I thought you were kinda scary,

00:16:15.330 --> 00:16:16.540
but you're actually nice!

00:16:16.540 --> 00:16:19.040
Wh-What are you talking about?

00:16:19.040 --> 00:16:21.170
She's a drama queen!

00:16:21.170 --> 00:16:23.300
Where'd you learn that term?

00:16:23.630 --> 00:16:25.090
Let's play hide and seek!

00:16:25.090 --> 00:16:25.880
Tag!

00:16:25.880 --> 00:16:27.840
Red light, green light!

00:16:27.840 --> 00:16:29.430
Wait—Which is it?!

00:17:31.870 --> 00:17:34.530
S-Sorry to keep you waiting!

00:17:35.530 --> 00:17:37.080
Finally!

00:17:37.080 --> 00:17:38.950
Where did you go?!

00:17:38.950 --> 00:17:40.580
Oh, right!

00:17:40.580 --> 00:17:42.710
I bought a few things.

00:17:43.170 --> 00:17:45.290
Some yummy snacks!

00:17:45.290 --> 00:17:48.090
Shopping, huh? Well, aren't you special?

00:17:48.090 --> 00:17:50.920
I'm not... I'm really not...

00:17:50.920 --> 00:17:53.670
You have no idea what I've been through.

00:17:54.170 --> 00:17:57.090
These kids I don't even know asked me to play,

00:17:57.090 --> 00:17:58.850
and I couldn't say no...

00:17:59.520 --> 00:18:02.100
And then they just vanished.

00:18:02.100 --> 00:18:02.850
Huh?

00:18:03.270 --> 00:18:05.470
They just left without saying a word.

00:18:05.470 --> 00:18:08.360
Kids these days are so rude.

00:18:09.470 --> 00:18:11.690
And it'll be dark soon.

00:18:12.190 --> 00:18:14.440
They'd better have gotten home safely.

00:18:15.440 --> 00:18:19.040
So, why did you go out to buy snacks, anyway?

00:18:24.290 --> 00:18:27.420
It's an offering... for the children.

00:18:30.920 --> 00:18:32.460
If...

00:18:33.680 --> 00:18:36.600
And I mean <i>if</i> the sixth sense is real,

00:18:36.600 --> 00:18:38.260
what good is it?

00:18:39.560 --> 00:18:43.440
All it does is scare people
and place more burdens on you.

00:18:43.440 --> 00:18:45.560
There's nothing good about it.

00:18:46.270 --> 00:18:47.400
Inoue.

00:18:47.970 --> 00:18:48.970
What?

00:18:49.570 --> 00:18:53.230
These offerings don't ever go away.

00:18:53.230 --> 00:18:54.280
Huh?

00:18:54.280 --> 00:18:56.450
Of course they don't.

00:18:56.450 --> 00:18:59.450
You can't eat when you're dead.

00:18:59.830 --> 00:19:02.160
Yes... You're right.

00:19:04.080 --> 00:19:07.460
But I can see them.

00:19:08.420 --> 00:19:12.630
I see them happily eating the offerings.

00:19:16.800 --> 00:19:19.010
It's not a one-way street.

00:19:19.670 --> 00:19:22.760
Everyone, alive or dead,

00:19:23.380 --> 00:19:25.680
shares a bond through the same feelings.

00:19:28.350 --> 00:19:33.230
And through my sixth sense,
I can confirm those bonds are real.

00:19:34.770 --> 00:19:40.570
Ever since I was little, this power
has helped me form many bonds.

00:19:41.820 --> 00:19:43.070
It still does.

00:19:44.360 --> 00:19:48.490
It created a chance for me to talk with you.

00:19:51.160 --> 00:19:52.990
It helped us grow

00:19:53.910 --> 00:19:55.260
a little closer.

00:19:57.130 --> 00:20:02.640
I-I'm sorry! I'm getting full of myself!

00:20:03.310 --> 00:20:08.140
I shouldn't assume that we're on friendly terms...

00:20:10.110 --> 00:20:12.190
Bonds, huh?

00:20:24.450 --> 00:20:25.540
Um...

00:20:26.080 --> 00:20:28.670
I-Is something wrong?

00:20:29.370 --> 00:20:32.130
I was just resigning myself. Don't worry about it.

00:20:43.710 --> 00:20:45.520
Okay then.

00:20:46.310 --> 00:20:50.520
It's about to get really dark. Let's head home...

00:20:53.110 --> 00:20:54.020
Amami.

00:20:56.190 --> 00:20:58.280
Inoue, did you just...

00:20:58.700 --> 00:21:01.320
Shut up! Let's just go, Amami!

00:21:02.530 --> 00:21:03.280
Okay!

00:21:05.330 --> 00:21:08.330
Come play with us again, okay?

00:21:10.920 --> 00:21:13.990
Hey, did you say something?

00:21:13.990 --> 00:21:15.170
No.

00:21:16.130 --> 00:21:17.260
But...

00:21:18.630 --> 00:21:22.390
I just saw another beautiful bond form.

00:21:28.970 --> 00:21:32.940
Why'd you want to walk home with me, anyway?

00:21:33.470 --> 00:21:35.270
W-Well...

00:21:35.270 --> 00:21:36.570
It's love!

00:21:38.070 --> 00:21:41.480
I-It's not! I just wanted to talk a little more...

00:21:41.480 --> 00:21:42.450
A-Are you talking to that cat?

00:21:42.450 --> 00:21:44.070
So it's not... um...

00:21:44.070 --> 00:21:44.570
A-Are you talking to that cat?

00:21:45.080 --> 00:21:48.200
Oh, yeah, I can talk to cats.

00:21:48.200 --> 00:21:51.830
And this cat isn't just an ordinary cat—

00:21:51.830 --> 00:21:54.460
No! I don't wanna hear it!

00:21:54.460 --> 00:21:55.090
I see 'em!

00:21:55.090 --> 00:21:55.500
No! I don't wanna hear it!

00:21:55.500 --> 00:21:57.460
P-Please, wait!

00:21:57.460 --> 00:22:00.220
Like I'm gonna wait just because you tell me to!

00:22:00.220 --> 00:22:01.800
Please don't say that!

00:22:01.800 --> 00:22:02.720
Stay away from me!

00:22:02.720 --> 00:22:03.130
Please wait! Please!

00:22:03.130 --> 00:22:04.430
Go away!

00:22:04.430 --> 00:22:05.300
Please wait! Please!

00:22:05.300 --> 00:22:06.390
I said stay away!

00:22:06.390 --> 00:22:09.430
Girl-on-girl lovin'. Heh.

00:23:41.520 --> 00:23:43.530
Good evening. I'm Amami Hibiki.

00:23:43.990 --> 00:23:47.780
If you stay up too late, it'll be hard to wake up in the morning.

00:23:47.780 --> 00:23:49.780
Please be careful, everyone.

00:23:50.410 --> 00:23:53.740
I'm a bit sleep-deprived myself...

00:23:53.750 --> 00:23:56.790
It's not that I was up late, but I just...

00:23:56.790 --> 00:24:00.790
It's embarrassing to say, but a lot happened.

